cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The Finite Element Method for the One-Dimensional Wave Equation
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying report, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nông
    given-names: Thanh Toàn
  - family-names: Nguyễn
    given-names: Hoàng Tú
abstract: >-
  P1 finite elements with leapfrog time stepping for the 1-D wave equation,
  written around the sharp stability constant. The familiar CFL condition
  Δt ≤ h/c is not sufficient with a consistent mass matrix; the closed-form
  spectrum of the generalised eigenproblem (S, T) gives the necessary and
  sufficient threshold Δt < 2/(c·√λmax), which is h/(c√3) for the full mass
  matrix and h/c for the lumped one. Every number published with the project
  is recomputed in CI.
keywords:
  - finite element method
  - wave equation
  - CFL condition
  - leapfrog scheme
  - mass lumping
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-29"
